__BBC Radio 4 (UK)__.  Michael Rosen's Word of Mouth series "took a journey into the world of words, language and the way we speak '.  The January 05, 2010 episode focused on constructed languages.  Lojban was featured along with Esperanto, Láadan and Klingon.  To hear a recording, including an interview with veteran lojbanist Colin Fine, download {file name="bbc4.ogg" page=>Multimedia showdesc=1}  


__Arika Okrent, Author of "In the Land of Invented Languages"__ (published March 24, 2009 by Spiegel & Grau) tells the fascinating and highly entertaining history of man’s enduring quest to build a better language.  To research her book and better understand Lojban, the author attended the Lojban Conference in 2006, and claims to have read all 600+ pages of the "The Complete Lojban Language".  There are many reviews of her book.  One such is to be found in the Aug 23, 2009 edition of [http://hestia.typepad.com/flatlander/2009/08/arika-okrent-in-the-land-of-invented-languages.html|Flatlander]. 


__Geoffrey Sampson, School of Cognitive and Computing Sciences, University of Sussex__ reviewed John Woldemar Cowan's "The Complete Lojban Language" in Journal of Linguistics 35.447–8, 1999.  Among others, he states: "In general, Lojban constitutes a strikingly thorough working-out of its creators’ goals, and its design is responsive to a rich, subtle understanding of linguistics and philosophical logic".  You can read the review [http://www.grsampson.net/VLoj.html|here].



__AI Expert Newsletter - March 2005__ looks at the history of Lojban and its predecessor Loglan, and discusses them from an AI perspective.  Read it [http://www.ainewsletter.com/newsletters/aix_0503.htm#loglan|here].




__J. Desquilbet, Staff, IBM, Software Group__ wrote an article entitled "Using UML to understand Lojban" for the Feb 05, 2004 edition of IBM's e-magazine Rational Edge. Unified Modeling Language (UML) is a standardized general-purpose modeling language used in the field of software engineering. You can find the article [http://www.ibm.com/developerworks/rational/library/2740.html|here].


